### Strangler migration — try it from VS Code (REST Client) or Rider/Visual Studio.
### Run it first: `docker compose up --build`. Dashboard: http://localhost:8080
@gateway = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Customers are already migrated → X-Served-By: modern
GET {{gateway}}/api/customers/1

### 2. Orders are in Shadow → X-Served-By: legacy, compared in the background
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/2

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders

### 3. What shadow traffic found (the legacy total truncates a cent)
GET {{gateway}}/migration/api/mismatches

### 4. Every route, its mode and counters
GET {{gateway}}/migration/api/routes

### 5. Canary: 30 % of order reads go to the modern service
PUT {{gateway}}/migration/api/routes/orders-read
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "Canary", "canaryPercent": 30 }

### 6. A canary key keeps one customer on the same side
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/1
X-Canary-Key: customer-42

### 7. Writes cannot be shadowed → 409
PUT {{gateway}}/migration/api/routes/orders-write
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "Shadow", "canaryPercent": 0 }

### 8. A write still goes to the legacy service…
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": 2, "items": [{ "product": "Pen", "quantity": 3, "unitPrice": 2.50, "discountPercent": 0 }] }

### 9. …and the modern read sees it (shared database, read-only)
PUT {{gateway}}/migration/api/routes/orders-read
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "Modern", "canaryPercent": 0 }

### 10. Roll back
PUT {{gateway}}/migration/api/routes/orders-read
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "Legacy", "canaryPercent": 0 }
